SeisBench picker for LOC-FLOW

This directory contains `runseisbench.py`, a SeisBench wrapper that writes
REAL-compatible pick files directly.

Default input layout:

    ../../Data/waveform_sac/YYYYMMDD/NET.STA.CHANNEL
    ../../Data/station.dat

If `../../Data/station.dat` does not exist, the script falls back to
`../../Data/station_all.dat`.

Default output layout:

    picks/PhaseNet_original/YYYYMMDD/NET.STA.P.txt
    picks/PhaseNet_original/YYYYMMDD/NET.STA.S.txt

Each pick line is:

    seconds_since_midnight probability amplitude

Basic usage:

    python3 runseisbench.py --models PhaseNet_original --start-date 2016-10-14 --nday 1 --device auto

Model and weight syntax:

    PhaseNet_original
    PhaseNet:original
    PhaseNet:stead
    EQTransformer:stead
    EQTransformer:stead@EQT_Ranked25_WOGrCl_Aug_0.3_2

The output folder label is normally `<Model>_<Weight>`. Use `@label` to set a
custom folder name.

CPU and GPU examples:

    python3 runseisbench.py --models PhaseNet_original --device cpu --workers 8
    python3 runseisbench.py --models PhaseNet_original --device cuda:0
    python3 runseisbench.py --models PhaseNet_original --device all --workers 2

Multiple models can be run together. Each model/weight pair gets its own pick
folder:

    python3 runseisbench.py --models PhaseNet_original,PhaseNet_stead,EQTransformer_stead --device auto

For OBS-style three-component files such as `DHZ`, `DH1`, and `DH2`, use exact
channels and a file template:

    python3 runseisbench.py \
      --data-dir /path/to/waveform_sac_withInstrument_Response_500HZ \
      --station-file /path/to/station_list_3Cs.json \
      --file-template "{date}/{station}/5B.{station}.{channel}" \
      --channels DHZ,DH1,DH2 \
      --start-date 2016-10-26 \
      --end-date 2016-12-01 \
      --models PhaseNet_original \
      --model-sampling-rate 500 \
      --device auto

CSV results are disabled by default because the REAL-ready pick files are
written directly. Enable CSV output only when needed:

    python3 runseisbench.py --models PhaseNet_original --save-csv

To associate SeisBench picks with REAL:

    cd ../../REAL
    perl runREAL.pl 3 PhaseNet_original

To use SeisBench through `run_all.sh`, set:

    picker=3
    seisbench_model=PhaseNet_original
